WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.314 --> 00:00:02.080
(calm music)

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.500
- [Narrator] SUPERBOWL
56 is the first time

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.360
that cryptocurrency
companies will be advertising

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.220
on the largest stage in the world.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:11.740
- This moment with these
companies buying ads

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:12.573
in the SUPERBOWL,

00:00:12.573 --> 00:00:16.400
sort of caps off what
has been a long run up

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.650
for the cryptocurrency sector

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:22.730
in terms of its mainstream
recognition and acceptance.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:26.630
And now what you are going to
see probably with these ads

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:30.640
is that this is a real
sort of unveiling moment

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.270
for this entire sector.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:33.460
- I've missed out on a lot,

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:35.640
but I am not gonna miss out on this.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.490
- [Narrator] So, which companies are vying

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:40.030
for Americans' attention
this football Sunday?

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:42.580
And what can we expect from the big game's

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.400
new crypto advertisers?

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.330
- FTX is giving away the time.
Their ad runs in Bitcoin.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.900
- [Narrator] Today, watching
SUPERBOWL commercials

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.710
is arguably as much of
an American tradition

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:54.197
as watching the game itself.

00:00:54.197 --> 00:00:57.260
- So SUPERBOWL Sunday is the
most expensive real estate

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:58.410
on all of television.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.270
If you have a company that's new

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.160
and you wanna cement it's brand name

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.640
like become the next Budweiser,
or the next Coca-Cola,

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.230
you need those eyeballs.

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:10.160
- [Narrator] In 2022,
each 30-second ad slot

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:11.823
went for as much as $7 million,

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.533
up from $5.6 million last year.

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:19.700
- This year, we are going to
be calling this the Crypto Bowl

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:23.340
because there are a
slew of crypto companies

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:25.060
that are going to be advertising

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:26.940
in the game and around the game.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:31.190
- [Narrator] Crypto Bowl, is
a play on the .combowl of 2000

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:34.900
which saw ads from a slew
of internet related brands,

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.597
many of which went on to fail.

00:01:36.597 --> 00:01:39.980
(bright music)

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:44.090
- What we know right now
is that three companies

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:45.650
are going to be running ads

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:48.200
in the broadcast of the game itself,

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.060
and they're all exchanges.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:55.610
They are COINBASE, FTX, and CRYPTO.COM.

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:57.570
- Fortune favors the brave.

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:59.780
- [Narrator] So far,
none of those companies

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:02.530
have shared much about
their upcoming commercials.

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:05.440
- The Crypto companies have
been particularly secretive

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:06.530
about what they're gonna do

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:07.970
with their advertising this year.

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:11.540
They definitely or probably
will rely on big celebrities,

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:15.040
'cause that seems to be what
most businesses that are new

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:15.873
try to do.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.420
- History is filled with almost.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:23.250
- [Narrator] Last October,
CRYPTO.COM released an ad

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:24.540
featuring Matt Damon.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.789
- You know what? I'm in.

00:02:25.789 --> 00:02:27.820
- [Narrator] In its past campaigns,

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:31.520
rival exchange FTX featured Tom Brady.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.240
A fourth cryptocurrency exchange, BINANCE,

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:37.520
is pursuing a more
unconventional strategy.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.580
BINANCE will run an ad
campaign around the game

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:43.450
